From c4464cfaa8326730b7704838176fcd8fe5334481 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:39:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] 0167: shop character rows + Luigi icon (v1 shop picker
 data)

ItemList.szs: three common character rows at BYML 0,1,2 (Mario, Luigi,
Wario; ItemType Clothes, Price 0, no StoreName), so they are the first
three filtered rows in every shop. Rebuilt with the in-place SARC
builder (data_off and 0x80 alignment preserved); re-parse confirms
rows 3-149 are the original 147 rows in order.

SystemMessage.szs: ItemCloth.msbt gains 4 labels (Luigi, Luigi_Explain,
Wario, Wario_Explain) reusing existing TXT2 text indices; TXT2 is
byte-identical. Mario needs no new label.

Luigi2D.szs: new shop icon for the Luigi row, built the same way as the
overlay Wario2D.szs (SARC of InitAudio.byml + a BFRES whose FMDL is
renamed to Mario2D); source is Luigi.szs's Mario.bfres.

Note: the shop-picker write-back (0166) is not in this commit; it is
blocked on identifying the confirmed row (see the game note).
